.\" $OpenBSD$
.\" Public domain.
.Dd $Mdocdate: September 5 2026 $
.Dt MOUNT_BTRFS 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mount_btrfs
.Nd mount a Btrfs file system
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl d Ar device
.Op Fl o Ar options
.Op Fl s Ar subvolid
.Ar special node
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
command attaches the Btrfs file system on the device
.Ar special
to the file system namespace at
.Ar node .
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl d Ar device
Supply an additional member of a multi-device file system.
Repeat this option for each member other than
.Ar special .
All members must be supplied for the first mount, in any order.
Up to 64 members are supported.
The driver supports SINGLE and DUP profiles; both copies of a DUP
chunk reside on the same member.
Missing members and RAID profiles are not supported.
.It Fl o Ar options
Specify a comma-separated list of mount options.
See
.Xr mount 8
for the available options.
.It Fl s Ar subvolid
Select an existing subvolume by its numeric tree ID.
The default, also selected by zero or 5, is the top-level tree.
The on-disk default subvolume setting is not used.
.El
.Pp
Multiple mounts of the same file system may be writable simultaneously if
their selected subvolume hierarchies are disjoint.
A selected tree cannot equal, contain, or be contained by another
mounted tree.
In particular, a top-level mount excludes all other mounts of that file system.
Nested subvolumes remain accessible through their containing mount,
and each subvolume's read-only flag is honored.
.Pp
Later mounts may name any member of the mounted file system without
repeating the
.Fl d
options.
Mounts of one file system share allocation and a transaction.
Syncing or unmounting any view may commit changes made through other views.
All member devices remain open until the last view is unmounted.
A read-only view may join a filesystem opened writable.
If the first view was read-only, all views must be unmounted before
mounting a writable view.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Mount a file system with three members:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# mount_btrfs -d /dev/sd2c -d /dev/sd3c /dev/sd1c /mnt/btrfs
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mount 2 ,
.Xr fstab 5 ,
.Xr mount 8 ,
.Xr umount 8
.Sh CAVEATS
The driver supports a limited subset of Btrfs formats and write operations.
Mount updates and online device addition, removal, and balancing are
not supported.
